atlas settlement

# Where this institution settles payment, declared once.
#
# Five commerce grammars quote the same capabilities -- x402, MPP, UCP, ACP and
# Beckn -- and each used to state its own settlement rail in its own emitter.
# Beckn stated none at all, so it quoted an amount an agent had no way to pay.
# Four separate string literals in one file was already drift waiting to happen;
# a second organ asserting its own rail would be drift nobody could see.
#
# This file is the source. `cmd/BonfyreAtlas/bonfyre-atlas compile-contracts settlement` renders
# it into cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/bf_settlement.h, and the surface test fails
# if the header and this contract disagree. Changing where payment settles is an
# edit here, not an edit in every carrier that mentions it.
#
# Cannot infer: a declared rail is not a configured one. This says where payment
# would settle. Whether it can settle is the x402 requirements block's answer,
# and while payTo, asset and facilitator are unset that answer is no -- for all
# five carriers at once, because all five render this one declaration.

settlement_contract commerce
  rail x402
  quote_path /mpp/quote
  discovery_path /capability
  carrier x402
  carrier MPP
  carrier UCP
  carrier ACP
  carrier Beckn
  forbidden_inference a declared settlement rail -> a configured one, a settled payment, or a reserved organ
